course: dictionary
lesson: 8316
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word robin can be a bird, a name, or a hero in a story. Read the words around it and ask: which meaning fits here?
explain: «That cheerful robin is also one of the fiercest birds in the garden.» The garden and the bird clues show that robin means a small bird with a red breast. «The scientist Robin Dunbar suggested...» has a capital R and a surname after it, so here robin is a person's first name.
explain: «Robin Hood» is a famous hero of old English stories, and «Robin is also Batman's helper» uses it as a name too. When you meet robin, swap your meaning into the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: A robin is a small bird with a red or orange breast.
fact: Robin is also a name for a boy or a girl.
fact: Robin Hood is a famous hero of old English stories.
fact: American robins are bigger than European robins, and they are a kind of thrush.
fact: American robins lay blue eggs and eat worms.
exercise: «Start digging in a garden and a robin will often hop down beside your spade within minutes.» What is a robin in this sentence? | A tool for digging | A hero of old stories | *A small bird | A person's first name
exercise: In «The scientist Robin Dunbar suggested a person can keep about 150 close relationships», what is Robin? | *A person's first name | A type of game | A bird with a red breast | A tree in the garden
exercise: In the stories, Robin Hood took from the rich to give to the poor. What kind of character is he? | A scientist | A bird | *A hero | A cook
test: What colour are the eggs of an American robin? | White | Green | *Blue | Red
test: According to the sentences, what do robins eat? | Seeds from the bins | Fish from the pond | *Worms and grubs | Bread from people's hands
exam: In which sentence does robin mean a small bird? | «Robin Dunbar is a scientist.» | «Robin Hood helped the poor.» | *«A robin hopped down beside the spade.» | «Robin and Sam went home.»
